-- title:
--   Mackey decomposition for coinduction from a normal subgroup
-- statement:
--   Let $k$ be a commutative ring and $V$ a $k$-module, let $\Gamma$ and $G$ be groups, let $r \colon G \to \Gamma$ be a group homomorphism and let $U \le \Gamma$ be a normal subgroup. Write $N = U \sqcup \operatorname{range} r$ for the subgroup of $\Gamma$ generated by $U$ and the image of $r$ (so $N = U\,r(G)$, as $U$ is normal), and suppose given a function $\gamma \colon \Gamma/N \to \Gamma$ which is a set-theoretic section of the canonical projection, i.e. the class of $\gamma(t)$ in $\Gamma/N$ is $t$ for every $t$. Consider the $\Gamma$-representation $P = \operatorname{coind}_{U \hookrightarrow \Gamma}$ of the trivial $U$-module $V$, restricted along $r$ to a $G$-representation, and the $G$-representation $Q = \operatorname{coind}_{r^{-1}(U) \hookrightarrow G}$ of the trivial $r^{-1}(U)$-module of functions $\Gamma/N \to V$. The assertion is that there exists a $k$-linear isomorphism $e$ from the underlying module of $\operatorname{Res}_r P$ to that of $Q$ which (i) intertwines the actions, $e(\rho_{\operatorname{Res}_r P}(g) f) = \rho_Q(g)(e f)$ for all $g \in G$, and (ii) is given by the explicit formula $(e f)(h)(t) = f(\gamma(t)\, r(h))$ for all $f$, all $h \in G$ and all $t \in \Gamma/N$, where $f$ is viewed as a function $\Gamma \to V$ and $e f$ as a function $G \to (\Gamma/N \to V)$.
--
--   This is Mackey's double coset formula for the restriction along $r$ of a module coinduced from a normal subgroup: all the subgroups $r^{-1}(\gamma^{-1} U \gamma)$ attached to the double cosets coincide with $r^{-1}(U)$, so the (possibly infinite) sum over $U \backslash \Gamma / r(G) = \Gamma/U\,r(G)$ is packaged as a single coinduced module of functions on that quotient, with the isomorphism given by an explicit formula rather than merely abstractly. It is used in the comparison of restriction and coinduction on degree-two cocycles and coboundaries, by [`groupCohomology.exists_mem_levelCocycles2_res_coind_apply_eq`](thm.html#groupCohomology.exists_mem_levelCocycles2_res_coind_apply_eq) and [`groupCohomology.res_coind_mem_levelCoboundaries2_of_forall_apply_mem_levelCoboundaries2`](thm.html#groupCohomology.res_coind_mem_levelCoboundaries2_of_forall_apply_mem_levelCoboundaries2).
